"Spell impressions are System-granted spells, earned by leveling or given as special rewards."
"Some classes have soft restrictions on them; some System spells may be reserved for S-ranks."
"Impressions are transferred directly into the brain."
"Every spell needs deliberate casting: magic words, gestures, chants or wands."
"A B-rank pre-affixation choice is one F-rank spell or one high-complexity D-rank."
"A noisemaker bang at a set distance and direction is common among heroes."
"Haunting Sphere, a complex D-rank, makes a Temper Sphere turn invisible and scream."
"Temper Spheres are glass balls of glitter dirt sold for 200 Argold in Anesidoran Wright shops."
"Impressions are almost always weaker than equivalently ranked skills."
"An impression is a perfect copy of a real spell, its casting instructions impressed unerringly."
"Real wizard spells cannot be learned by mimicry and are exponentially harder for non-Artonans."
"A few trinket spells are easy enough for non-Artonans to learn."
